213:- `total_fill_wall_ns`/`decode_fill_wall_ns`: main-thread wall time inside `fill()` (job building, mincore, wait). `demand_wait_ns_total` equals `total_fill_wall_ns`; `demand_wait_ns_per_token = total / expert_demand_tokens` (decode tokens when MAX_TOKENS=1).
215:Pregate (`expert_pregate: stats`, `llama-context.cpp:871-893`), exact line:
216:`expert_pregate: stats predictions= arrivals= hits= actual= predicted= recall_at_k= precision= async_bytes_read= async_reads= async_errors= dropped= cancelled_jobs= cancelled_bytes= inflight_at_arrival= inflight_reads= pending_reads= sync_bytes_with_prediction= sync_bytes_without_prediction= sync_calls_with_prediction= sync_calls_without_prediction= skips= pred_done= pred_inflight= pred_queued= pred_resident_at_predict= hit_done= hit_inflight= hit_queued= hit_resident= recall_at_k_d1= recall_at_k_d2= actual_d1= actual_d2= hits_d1= hits_d2= demand_wait_ns_total= demand_wait_ns_per_token=`
230:- (b) "its bytes were resident before demand": partly. Closest are `hit_done` (+`hit_inflight` partial), `hit_resident` (resident BEFORE any pregate IO, so not credited to pregate), and the change in `decode_bytes_read` / `bytes_skipped_resident` / `sync_bytes_with_prediction` versus a fill-only baseline run.
231:  `bytes_skipped_resident` alone cannot attribute residency to prediction versus natural page-cache retention from earlier tokens. `hit_done` is an I/O-state classification, not a residency measurement: it is not re-validated by `mincore` at arrival/demand; with `DIAG=1`, `pre_use_nonresident` is a residency measurement but only after the demand fill, and not split by predicted/unpredicted.
232:- (c) fewer page faults vs lower decode time: not separable without DIAG. Without DIAG there is no fault counter at all in the engine and no per-token or per-layer wall time split; `demand_wait_ns_per_token` captures only time blocked in `fill()`. Fault counts (`majflt_between`, `minflt_between`) exist only in DIAG runs (which add cuts, getrusage and mincore overhead).
260:12. `expert_demand_tokens` counts filled-ubatch tokens only; with MIN/MAX changes `demand_wait_ns_per_token` denominators change meaning.

